{"Background": ("Tandy Bowen grew up in an affluent but emotionally cold household in Shaker Heights, Ohio. Her father abandoned the family, and her mother, a self-absorbed socialite, provided little emotional support. Craving love and connection, Tandy fled to New York City at 16, seeking a fresh start. There, she met Tyrone Johnson, a kindred spirit and fellow runaway. Their lives took a dark turn when they were kidnapped by criminals testing a mix of heroin and experimental drugs. While the drugs killed most victims, Tandy and Tyrone survived, their latent mutant abilities activated. Tandy gained the power to create and project light daggers, symbolizing her inner purity. Together with Tyrone, now Cloak, she became one half of the vigilante duo Cloak and Dagger, dedicated to battling crime and protecting the vulnerable.")}

{"Description": ("Tandy Bowen, known as Dagger, has recently continued honing her powers and reaffirmed her commitment to protecting those in need. After a period of personal turmoil and distance from Cloak, she reconnected with Tyrone and reestablished their unique partnership. She has taken a more proactive role in fighting human trafficking and drug-related crimes, aligning herself with various street-level heroes in New York City. While still plagued by doubts stemming from her early life, she has grown more confident and independent, no longer defined solely by her relationship with Cloak. Tandy has also been involved in larger Marvel events, collaborating with teams like the Runaways and even aiding the Avengers when their causes align. Her mastery over her light daggers has improved, allowing for more controlled healing and targeted purification. Now a symbol of hope and resilience, Dagger stands as a more seasoned, focused hero than ever before.")}

{"Luminescent Pendant": "A small, tear-shaped crystal pendant that softly glows with an inner light. When worn around Tandy’s neck, it quietly collects and stores a portion of her radiant energy over time. By channeling the energy within the pendant, Tandy can maintain her full spectrum of abilities without relying on Cloak’s presence. Similarly, Cloak can draw upon the pendant’s stored light when Tandy isn’t nearby, keeping his darkness in check and allowing him to continue operating effectively on his own. After a dangerous encounter with a mystic-powered drug cartel, both Tandy and Tyrone realized the vulnerability of their reliance on one another’s presence. Seeking a solution, they consulted Doctor Strange, who forged the Luminescent Pendant from a shard of enchanted crystal. Gifted to Tandy, this pendant now ensures that both she and Cloak can stand strong, whether fighting side-by-side or walking their own paths.")}]
